    "body": "Landed in a worktree, staged but not committed (main session reviews and commits):\n\n- **Rotary Parallel**: when the centre-cutting guard retries with sloped entries on (`entry_ramp`), each radial infeed (the opening one and every link) becomes a straight ramp. It starts on the retract cylinder in the landing's meridian and descends while moving along the axis in the pass's own direction, at the finish's ramp angle (capped at 45 deg). Each ramp is proved clear of the part before it is used (`multiaxis/entry_ramp.rs::segment_clear`, ball centre sampled with a Lipschitz margin). An infeed with no proof keeps the radial plunge, and the guard refuses it by name. Under the retry the laid raster's upright-tool verbs (diagonal hops, ring entry ramps) are turned off, and a run's leading steep drop is dropped, because posed radially those run down the tool's own axis.\n- **Swarf**: under the retry, the first raster drop becomes an air drop to Top of Part Z behind the first line's start, then a ramp down the line's tangent onto it (same proof, posed by the stamp with the cut it lands into). With no room it drops straight and the guard judges it. Both cases leave a note.\n- With the guard's retry off (centre-cutting tools, and the default params) the output is byte-identical: golden_cl, rotary_verify and rotary_fixtures are green with no re-bless.\n- Still open (outside this issue): Swarf's link-swing re-entries can still plunge (the swarf air-link / re-entry audit item that is already owed), and the guard refuses those by name.\n\nTests: `entry_ramp::tests::{the_lipschitz_proof_passes_air_and_fails_a_gouge, swarf_first_entry_leads_in_down_the_lines_tangent_or_stays_put}`, `center_cut_multiaxis::{the_rotary_twins_under_the_forced_ramp_retry (re-pinned), swarf_first_entry_ramps_under_the_forced_retry}`.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
